sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Caller
  participant API as Control API
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant Worker as Orchestrator
  participant Provider as Provider gRPC
  participant Adapter as Fake or Proxmox

  Caller->>API: POST create or CreateInstance + OIDC token
  API->>API: Verify JWT, project grant, fields, idempotency key
  API->>DB: Begin acceptance transaction
  DB->>DB: Lock idempotency scope and network pool
  DB->>DB: Reserve quota and IPv4 address
  DB->>DB: Insert instance, operation, audit, outbox, projections
  DB-->>API: Commit durable intent
  API-->>Caller: 202 Accepted + operation ID

  loop Ordered Phase 3 polling until terminal
    Worker->>DB: Claim command or ready workflow
    DB->>DB: Acquire instance lease and increment fencing token
    DB-->>Worker: Command + persisted stage
    Worker->>DB: Persist pre-call or result checkpoint
    Worker->>Provider: Phase 3 provider RPC with stable request ID
    Provider->>Adapter: Provider-neutral port call
    Adapter-->>Provider: Accepted task, success, rejection, or observation
    Provider-->>Worker: Provider-neutral result
    Worker->>DB: Persist task reference, next stage, and workflow event
  end

  Worker->>Provider: ObserveInstance with expected ownership
  Provider->>Adapter: Read resource state and markers
  Adapter-->>Provider: Exists + running + exact marker match
  Provider-->>Worker: Authoritative observation
  Worker->>DB: Complete workflow and emit terminal event
  API->>DB: Apply ordered event to read projection
  Caller->>API: GET operation and instance
  API->>DB: Read project-scoped projections
  DB-->>API: succeeded operation + active instance
  API-->>Caller: Desired and observed state

  Note over Worker,DB: Kafka is intentionally absent in Phase 3. Polling is replaced by Debezium and Kafka in Phase 4.
